<div class="callout-text"><strong>Recruiting reality at 16:</strong> Most college scouts evaluating 16-year-olds for skill positions want to see <strong>4.6 seconds or faster</strong> to begin seriously tracking a prospect for D1 programs. For mid-major D1 and D2, 4.7 to 4.75 at 16 with room to develop is competitive. Scouts know you are 16 — they are projecting your speed at 18, not just reading today's number.</div>
